# Documentation Standards

## Go comments
- All exported types, functions, and constants have GoDoc comments
- Comments start with the symbol name: `// Proxy handles...`
- Comments explain WHAT it does, not HOW

## Markdown
- README.md sections: Overview, Install, Configuration, Usage, Contributing
- Each implemented spec gets a status update: `[x] Done` + link to PR
- CHANGELOG.md follows Keep a Changelog (https://keepachangelog.com)

## Inline comments
- Inline comments only for non-obvious logic
- Do not comment what the code does — comment WHY it does it that way

## Language
- All documentation, README files, and code comments must be written in English
